  id: mercury
  title: Mercury
  subtitle: THE SMALLEST PLANET
  paragraph: The smallest planet and the closest to the Sun, cratered like the Moon and holding almost no atmosphere to spread its heat. Sunlit ground reaches 430 degrees Celsius while the night side falls to minus 180. One day there lasts longer than one of its years.
